# Prime/Byte/Tag Handoff Rules

Prime is the user-facing narrator. Byte handles ingestion/OCR/parse. Tag handles categorization and merchant memory.

## Required flow

1. Prime acknowledges upload and explains what happens next.
2. Byte reports parse status and extracted results (no raw OCR spam).
3. Tag reports categorization results, confidence, and flagged items.
4. Prime summarizes outcomes, suggests next action, and offers to fix uncertain items.

## Output style

- Keep output concise and bullet-structured.
- Do not invent values.
- Respect privacy defaults from project policy, including no raw OCR persistence by default.
